accinated  about half a million of those people for  the first time  i'm hopeful that people are beginning to  realize how essential it is  doctors are telling americans vaccines  remain their best protection  currently 97 percent of all  hospitalizations  and 99 percent of all deaths from coba  19  are among the unvaccinated jennifer  johnson global news  washington kovat 19 continues to cast a  shadow over the olympics  new daily cases in host city tokyo just  hit a record high  4058 that didn't deter people from  defying a ban on spectators at the  olympics  crowds of masked fans gathered to watch  the triathlon mixed relay race  241 covet cases have been linked to the  games  so far coming up the canadian companies  offering persuasive perks  to battle a labor shortage  canada's economy is slowly reopening yet  many industries still face a labor  shortage  the pandemic is allowing a lot of  workers to rethink the jobs they have  and the ones they really want  and that's forcing companies to go above  and beyond to retain or attract them  and gaviola explains what some firms are  offering employees to stay  or to hop on board this is the  three-bedroom  fifteen hundred square foot house that  thirty-year-old ian balecta is moving  into with his girlfriend  this first home purchase made possible  with a twenty thousand dollar bonus from  the company he works for  the catch he has to stay with the  company for at least three years  we're excited it's hard to describe  right when you've been waiting so long  to own a home and find the time is here  in a tight labor market incentives like  this go a long way  when we went into the brainstorming  sessions for this program we really  wanted to make it impactful  you know more than an extra day of  holiday a recent survey by staffing firm  robert half shows the companies are  going the extra mile to attract workers  forty percent are offering more paid  time off thirty seven percent better job  titles  and more than one in three are offering  signing bonuses it's one of the toughest  labor markets uh to hire great engineers  and what makes it tougher for us is  we're looking for the top  one percent within that pool laser  technologies is a tech firm with a twist  offering its staff the option to work  fully remotely and shoulder to shoulder  with co-workers as often as they want  the company headquarters will remain in  toronto but its traveling office will  change locations several times a year  our first countries costa rica in  addition at that  we're planning on uruguay the uae  and several other places in the u.s in a  job market like this the onus is on  employers to do everything they can to  make  work feel less like work across our team  of 60  people get multiple offers from you know  square  shopify facebook constantly with with  numbers that are astronomical  but beyond that you know what they  really care about is  do i get flexibility better benefits  more money and all kinds of perks  recruitment experts say the pandemic is  a chance for workers in high demand  industries  to ask for exactly what they want  knowing that if they don't get it  other opportunities abound ann gaviola  global news  toronto still ahead  the highway that went nowhere and how it  sunk over a billion dollars along the  way  it's costing montenegro more than a  billion dollars to build one of the  world's most expensive highways  the tiny balkan country has borrowed  most of that from china  doubling montenegro's state debt the  loan has left the country at the mercy  of beijing and desperate for a bailout  as redmond shannon explains building the  highway which doesn't even go anywhere  yet has far-reaching consequences  montenegro is a spectacular destination  it's easy to see why this nation relies  so heavily on tourism  so when the pandemic hit the  consequences of a government gamble to  boost the economy  came tumbling down the hillside it  immediately struggled to pay off a  billion 