 the excitement for canadian  swimmer kylie moss at the tokyo olympics  the 25 year old from ontario scored her  second silver medal at the summer games  this time in the women's 200-meter  backstroke it's the fifth medal that  canadian women have won  in the pool moss's silver brings  canada's middle count to 12  and that puts us 12th in the overall  standings with three golds  four silvers and five bronze medals  so what happens when the athletes are  finished their events under olympic  coveted protocols they must leave tokyo  within 48 hours after their competition  ends calgary's haley daniels is one of  the athletes who has touched down at  home  having made history kami kepke has more  [Applause]  she may not have won gold but haley  daniels will always be  first the calgarian is the first  canadian to compete in the inaugural  women's canoe slalom at the olympics  a victory in a decades-long fight for  gender equality in the sport  we can celebrate that we had one step  forward in the tokyo olympics  it was like paddling in a swimming pool  outside  with not a lot of refreshing moments  but i couldn't help but smile at the  start line  just knowing that that we were amongst  first  mom karen hadn't seen her daughter for  seven months but says haley's journey to  tokyo  started before she was even born we were  whitewater  canoeing down the kootenai river as i  was pregnant with her and it's very cold  down the kootenay and quite wild  and we chipped over and i just held on  to her and i said  it's okay we're going to be doing a lot  of this  after the whirlwind of the games seeing  family friends and the next generation  of athletes greet her at the airport is  as great as any prize daniels could ask  for  seeing them here today and the big  smiles on their face under their mask of  course  knowing that they're excited to get on  the water  i mean that makes it all worth it the  second i saw her i was just like  hopping with excitement i want to be  like him  i want to make it to the olympics if i  can  yeah that's my dream too haley's father  kimberly  is also making history as the first  openly transgender official  at an olympics while father and daughter  blaze trails they hope to see more  backing for women's sports year round  we need to support women and we need to  support women in sports specifically and  so  i am so happy that we're finding gender  equal but there's still work that needs  to be done  and when a canadian woman someday  meddles in see one slalom  it will be in part because of the path  daniels helped pave kami kepke  global news good for her  and that is global national for this  saturday night i'm eric sorenson  tonight york canada is the granite  shorelines of cranberry cove  not far from peggy's cove nova scotia  please keep sending your photos to  viewers at globalnational.com  and thanks for watching i'll be i'll see  you again tomorrow night  have a great night  you
 

